---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import snapshot from "../_data/snapshots/live-7d.json";
import type { Snapshot } from "../types";

const data = snapshot as Snapshot;
const topThree = data.leaderboard.slice(0, 3);
---
<Base title="Home">
  <div class="banner">
    <strong>Preview build.</strong> This site is built against dummy snapshot data while the
    upstream API ships. Numbers do not reflect real contributor activity yet.
  </div>

  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Trace Commons is a user-owned register of AI agent work. When an agent does work
    for you, it leaves a record of what actually happened: the tools it called, the
    places it failed, the result it gave back. Contributors run
    <a href="https://github.com/iqlusioninc/ironclaw">Ironclaw</a> locally to capture
    and scrub those records. Only the scrubbed envelope reaches a shared server,
    where two gates decide whether it is filed: one asks whether the record is
    genuinely different from everything already in the register; the other asks
    whether it is substantive work, not template-shaped filler. Both must pass.
    Frontier labs, auditors, and regulators can later query the register under
    selective disclosure.
  </p>
  <p>
    A <strong>Trace Credit</strong> is the signed, on-chain record that one of a
    contributor's submissions was accepted. Credits are non-transferable; they are
    how recognition flows back when buyers later pay to query the evidence. This
    site surfaces the public, opt-in slice of contributor activity: a leaderboard
    of people who have explicitly chosen to be visible, and aggregate corpus
    analytics protected by min-cell and noise guards.
  </p>

  <h2>Top contributors (last 7d)</h2>
  {topThree.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="muted">No public contributors yet.</p>
  ) : (
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>#</th>
          <th>Handle</th>
          <th>Score</th>
          <th>Accepted</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {topThree.map((entry) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{entry.rank}</td>
            <td><a href={`/contributors/${entry.display_handle}`}>{entry.display_handle}</a></td>
            <td>{entry.score.toFixed(1)}</td>
            <td>{entry.accepted_count}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  )}
  <p><a href="/leaderboard">See the full leaderboard →</a></p>

  <h2>How to join</h2>
  <p>
    The pilot is invite-only. If you have an invite code and a workload token from
    the pilot operator, the contributor-side setup is documented in
    <a href="https://github.com/TraceCommons/trace-commons-server/blob/main/docs/operator/pilot-contributor-onboarding.md">pilot-contributor-onboarding.md</a>.
    Once a few of your submissions have cleared both gates you can opt in to the public leaderboard.
  </p>
</Base>
